#presentation(size = "wide", background = "#f8fafc")

#slide[
  #box(name = "Results", position = { x = inch(0.6), y = inch(0.5), width = inch(5.8), height = inch(6.4) },
       fill = "#ffffff", border = { color = "#cbd5e1", width = pt(1) },
       text = { size = pt(16), margin = { left = pt(12), right = pt(12), top = pt(8), bottom = pt(4) } })[
    ## Quarterly results

    Revenue rose in every region, and the table gives the figures.

    | Region | Q1 | Q2 |
    |--------|----|----|
    | North  | 12 | 15 |
    | South  | 9  | 11 |

    - The north leads.
    - The south follows.

    #chart(kind = "column", data = { categories = { "North", "South" }, series = { { name = "Q2", values = { 15, 11 } } } })

    A closing remark below the chart.
  ]

  #box(position = { x = inch(6.9), y = inch(0.5), width = inch(5.8), height = inch(6.4) }, fit = "contain")[
    A picture with its caption beneath:

    #image("assets/evidence_stack.png", alt = "Evidence")

    *Figure 1.* The evidence stack.
  ]
]
